The attached image (Figure 2) illustrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles are retained at the injection site and cleared with time, without systemic distribution. Whole-mouse imaging (a) shows the fluorescent signal of Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 remaining localized at the calf muscle injection site for 21 days, with its intensity gradually decreasing. Panel (b) confirms that at Day 21, fluorescence is only detected at the injection sites, not in internal organs. Quantification (c) shows a rapid initial decrease in fluorescence intensity after 0h, followed by a moderate increase on day 2, and then a steady decline, with about 20% of the original signal detected by day 21, supporting its localized action and eventual clearance.